    {
      "id": "finding-1-5-the-kind-adds-a-multi-name-recursion-guard-and-a-vibe-specific-env-allowlist-the",
      "text": "The kind adds a multi-name recursion guard and a Vibe-specific env allowlist. The ancestor walk matches `vibe`, `vibe-rs` and `vibe-app-server` rather than the launcher alone, because the Python launcher execs away and a running Vibe appears as its Rust binary or app server. The env filter passes the `VIBE_` prefix plus the single key `MISTRAL_API_KEY`, treats `VIBE_HOME` as lineage state, and denies an inherited `VIBE_HOME` so a leaf cannot reach the operator's Vibe state. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts:77] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts:108] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts:174] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts:190] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts:199]",
